# PART 4: GROUPS START IMMEDIATELY

## 4.1 Remove the old full-group waiting rule

Remove all application logic, instructions, messages, and conditions that require every membership slot to be filled before a group starts.

Remove wording such as:

"The group starts when every number is taken."

Replace it with:

"Your group starts as soon as the first member joins. Other members can join while the group is active."

## 4.2 Start from member number 1

The creator becomes member number 1 and activates the group immediately.

The application must not wait for member number 2 or the final member.

As additional members join:
- Update the current membership count.
- Update the available slots.
- Show the group's current status.
- Apply the configured payment schedule to the relevant member.
- Update the group's progress in real time where supported.

Example:

A group supports 10 members.

The creator opens the group and becomes member #1.

The group immediately becomes active with 1 of 10 slots occupied.

A second user joins and becomes member #2.

The group remains active.

A third user joins and becomes member #3.

The group remains active.

This continues until all 10 slots have been allocated.

If only four members have joined, the group remains active with four occupied slots and six available slots.

## 4.3 Payment scheduling

Implement the existing business rules for payments without requiring a full group before payment activity can begin.

A member's payment obligations must follow the actual schedule associated with the selected speed and the member's position.

Do not invent a new payment amount or payment frequency.

Do not assume that a user's position automatically determines their final delivery date unless that is part of the verified business rules.

Display:
- Selected speed.
- Member number.
- Amount due.
- Payment frequency.
- Next payment date, when configured.
- Payment status.
- Relevant group terms.

Members must be able to understand their own payment obligations before confirming participation.

Joining a group must not trigger an undocumented charge.

If a payment provider is connected, use verified payment events to update payment status.

If a payment provider is not connected, do not present simulated payments as real transactions.

Clearly distinguish pending, successful, failed, refunded, and overdue payments.

## 4.4 Real-time updates

When a new member joins, update:
- Occupied slots.
- Available slots.
- Membership count.
- Member list, subject to privacy rules.
- Group status.
- Relevant moderator notifications.

Use the existing real-time infrastructure if available.

Otherwise, implement reliable refresh or polling behavior appropriate to the current technology stack.

Do not display fabricated members to make a group appear active.

